From: Marcin Krystianc <marcin.krystianc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SUNRPC: resend a request whose reply asked for a retry

When rpc_decode_header() gets a reply it treats as possibly garbled
(GARBAGE_ARGS, SYSTEM_ERR, an unparsable reply, or MSG_DENIED with
AUTH_BADCRED or AUTH_BADVERF), it decrements tk_garb_retry and sets
tk_action to call_encode, expecting the request to be encoded and sent
again. call_decode() then calls xprt_conditional_disconnect() when the
client has cl_discrtry set.

call_encode() encodes only when rpc_task_need_encode() says so. For a
task that was already sent with RPC_TASK_NO_RETRANS_TIMEOUT set, as
every NFSv4 task is, that requires xprt_request_need_retransmit(),
i.e. a connection that has already dropped. The disconnect is only
queued on xprtiod, so call_encode() usually runs first. The task then
skips the encode and the transmit, goes on to call_decode() with
rq_reply_bytes_recvd still set, and decodes the same rejected reply
again. Two more passes use up tk_garb_retry and the RPC fails, with
-EACCES for AUTH_BADCRED, without the request being sent a second
time.

Until commit cc204d01262a ("SUNRPC: Dequeue the request from the
receive queue while we're re-encoding"), the -EAGAIN case of
call_decode() cleared rq_reply_bytes_recvd itself. That commit moved
the clearing into rpc_xdr_encode(), which this path does not reach
because rpc_task_need_encode() returns false. Since then the rejected
reply is neither cleared nor replaced.

knfsd answers a request whose RPCSEC_GSS integrity checksum does not
verify with AUTH_BADCRED (SVC_GARBAGE in svc_process_common()). With
sec=krb5i, xfstests generic/761 changes an O_DIRECT write buffer while
the write is in flight, so some WRITEs reach the server with a
checksum that does not match the data. A resend computes a new
checksum and succeeds; a skipped one makes write() fail with EACCES.

Make xprt_request_need_retransmit() also return true when
xprt_request_data_received() says a reply has been received. Its only
caller is rpc_task_need_encode(), and call_encode() sees a received
reply only after rpc_decode_header() rejected it. rpc_xdr_encode()
clears rq_reply_bytes_recvd, so this only changes the paths that come
back to call_encode() after a reply was received.

Measured with generic/761 run 20 times over NFSv4.2 and sec=krb5i,
knfsd and the client in one UML kernel: 17 of 20 runs failed before
this change. The trace of each failure shows one rpc_xdr_sendto, one
server rpcgss_svc_mic GSS_S_BAD_SIG, two rpc__bad_creds and then
rpc_call_rpcerror with -13. In the WRITEs that recovered,
xprt_disconnect_done came before the retry and the request was sent
again. With this change all 20 runs passed: 353 WRITEs got a bad MIC,
each was rejected once and sent again, and no RPC failed with -13.

Fixes: cc204d01262a ("SUNRPC: Dequeue the request from the receive queue while we're re-encoding")

---
Open points before sending:

- The measurement above was taken with an earlier form of this change,
  which tested rq_reply_bytes_recvd directly in
  rpc_task_need_encode(). This form calls xprt_request_data_received()
  from xprt_request_need_retransmit() instead, which also requires
  RPC_TASK_NEED_RECV to be clear. It has not been built or run.
- The Fixes: tag comes from reading the diffs of cc204d01262a and of
  762e4e67b356 ("SUNRPC: Refactor RPC call encoding"), which added the
  RPC_TASK_NO_RETRANS_TIMEOUT term to rpc_task_need_encode(). No
  kernel before and after cc204d01262a was built or tested.
- call_status() also moves to call_encode() on transport errors. If a
  reply completes while the task is being woken with such an error,
  this change resends instead of decoding that reply. Before, it was
  decoded. Not observed; it needs a review.

diff --git a/net/sunrpc/xprt.c b/net/sunrpc/xprt.c
--- a/net/sunrpc/xprt.c
+++ b/net/sunrpc/xprt.c
@@ -1567,12 +1567,16 @@ xprt_request_prepare(struct rpc_rqst *re
  * xprt_request_need_retransmit - Test if a task needs retransmission
  * @task: pointer to rpc_task
  *
- * Test for whether a connection breakage requires the task to retransmit
+ * Test for whether a connection breakage requires the task to retransmit,
+ * or whether a reply has been received. call_encode() sees a received
+ * reply only after rpc_decode_header() rejected it with a request to
+ * retry, so the request must be encoded and sent again.
  */
 bool
 xprt_request_need_retransmit(struct rpc_task *task)
 {
-	return xprt_request_retransmit_after_disconnect(task);
+	return xprt_request_data_received(task) ||
+		xprt_request_retransmit_after_disconnect(task);
 }
 
